Lucky\") | ₹ 37,950 |\n| [Chandak Greenairy](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/chandak-greenairy/152458/project \"Chandak Greenairy\") | ₹ 37,100 |\n| [H Rishabraj Astral](https://www.squareyards.com/mumbai-residential-property/h-rishabraj-astral/325598/project \"H Rishabraj Astral\") | ₹ 30,900 |\n| Borivali West | ₹ 30,900 |\n| Current Project **Romell Ariana** | ₹ 30,600 |\n\n### Rentals\n\nMonthly Rent in Borivali West ranges from ₹ 22.1 K to ₹ 74.4 K with options available for STUDIO,1,2,3 BHK units\n\n| Configuration | In Romell Ariana | In Borivali West |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 BHK | - | ₹ 32.7 K |\n| 2 BHK | - | ₹ 45.5 K |\n| 3 BHK | - | ₹ 74.4 K |\n\n### Recent Updates\n\nGet the latest price and market updates for Romell Ariana.\n\n#### Mumbai's Water Stock at 95.97% with Seven Lakes Holding High Levels\n\nMumbai's water stock has reached 95.97%, with seven lakes maintaining high levels. This ensures a stable water supply for the city, though civic authorities continue to monitor reservoir levels and rainfall.\n\nA total of 5 residential transactions has been registered so far for Romell Ariana, amounting to ₹ 7 Cr till September 2026.\n\nDuring Q2'2026, average property prices for Romell Ariana moved from ₹ 30,350/sqft to ₹ 30,600/sqft, reflecting a 0.82% rise.\n\n#### MMRDA Presents Surplus Budget with Significant Allocation for Infrastructure\n\nMMRDA has presented a surplus budget of ₹48,072 crore, with 87% allocated to infrastructure projects, including roads, public transport, and urban development. A notable provision of ₹4,000 crore is earmarked for the development of Mumbai 3.0 New Town, aiming for planned urban expansion.\n\n#### BMC Budget Includes ₹6,475 Crore for Water Security Projects\n\nThe BMC's FY26-27 budget includes a substantial allocation of ₹6,475 crore for water security initiatives. This funding is designated for projects such as the Manori desalination plant (₹500 crore) and the Gargai project (₹437.51 crore), aimed at augmenting the city's water supply capacity.\n\n#### Mumbai-Pune Expressway 'Missing Link' Project Set for May 1 Inauguration, Promising Safer and Faster Travel\n\nThe highly anticipated 'Missing Link' project on the Mumbai-Pune Expressway is set to be inaugurated on May 1, significantly reducing travel time by approximately 30 minutes and enhancing safety. The 10.5-km stretch features tunnels and a bridge, bypassing the accident-prone Khandala Ghat. This infrastructure upgrade is expected to ease traffic congestion, improve travel safety.\n\nDuring Q1'2026, average property prices for Romell Ariana moved from ₹ 24,650/sqft to ₹ 30,350/sqft, reflecting a 23.12% rise.\n\n### Govt. Registrations\n\n5 Sales Transactions Registered in Romell Ariana From Oct 25 to Sep 26 at Avg. Price ₹ 31.5 K/Sq.Ft.\n\n| Sales Transactions | Gross Sales Value | Registered Rate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 5 | ₹ 7 Cr | ₹ 31,500 / Sq. Ft. |\n\nTransaction Period Oct 25 to Sep 26\n\n## Romell Ariana Floor Plans\n\n![Floor plan of 2 BHK 700 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Romell Ariana, Mumbai](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/unit-image/romell-ariana-apartment-2-bhk-682sqft-20254414164451-3d-5634.jpg?aio=w-278;h-200;crop;)\n\n### 2 BHK 700 Sq. Ft. Apartment\n\n(Carpet Area)\n\nPrice: **₹ 2.24 Cr**\n\n![Floor plan of 2 BHK 741 Sq. Ft. Apartment in Romell Ariana, Mumbai](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/unit-image/romell-ariana-apartment-2-bhk-741sqft-20254414164443-3d-4307.jpg?aio=w-278;h-200;crop;)\n\n### 2 BHK 741 Sq. Ft. Apartment\n\n(Carpet Area)\n\nPrice: **₹ 2.37 Cr**\n\n## Master Plan, Photos, Videos & Brochure of Romell Ariana\n\nExplore the master plan, project photos and walkthrough videos of Romell Ariana to understand the overall layout, tower placement, amenities, landscaped spaces and key highlights before making your buying decision.\n\n![Romell Ariana Tower View](https://static.squareyards.com/resources/images/mumbai/project-image/